\DOC X86_PROMOTE_RETURN_NOSTACK_TAC

\TYPE {X86_PROMOTE_RETURN_NOSTACK_TAC : thm -> thm -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Proves a top-level {ensures} specification for a stack-free x86 subroutine (one
that only pops a return address) from a specification of its body, either
closing the goal or leaving a residual goal about the event trace.

\DESCRIBE
{mc : thm} names (or gives the byte-list definition of) the full machine-code
program appearing in the goal; {core : thm} is the correctness/safety theorem
for the body of that program, stated with {BUTLAST} of the code and an explicit
end-of-body program counter. The goal it is applied to has no assumptions and
is a universally quantified (optionally also existentially quantified over an
event function) implication whose antecedent is a conjunction or
{ALL (nonoverlapping ...)} list of separation and alignment side conditions,
and whose conclusion is an {ensures} triple for the whole program, with pre-
and postconditions referring to the stack pointer and return address. In many
cases the goal is closed outright, producing no subgoals; otherwise exactly one
subgoal remains:
{
   ?- t
   ========================================  X86_PROMOTE_RETURN_NOSTACK_TAC mc core
   A ?- u
}
\noindent Here all the universal variables have been stripped; {A} collects the
side conditions of the antecedent in expanded form ({nonoverlapping} unfolded
to {nonoverlapping_modulo} on the word values, and {LENGTH} of the code
evaluated to a numeral), the instantiated conclusions of {core} (including the
memory-access-bounds fact and, when {core} is existentially quantified over an
event function, an equation naming a witness function), and assumptions
describing two states: code loaded, the saved return address, a {MAYCHANGE}
relation between them, and the resulting program counter, stack pointer and
event list. The remaining conclusion {u} is the existential event-trace
statement from the postcondition, with the event list instantiated to the
concrete trace built from the body's events, a stack load and a jump.

\COMMENTS
The observed traces show only these two outcomes, always starting from
assumption-free goals of this {ensures}-promotion shape.

\ENDDOC
